# Redis accounts for the helpdesk. Install as /etc/redis/users.acl, owned
# by redis:redis, mode 0600. Replace CHANGE-ME with a long random
# password (python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))")
# and put the same password in the helpdesk credential file:
#
#     redis+unix://helpdesk:<password>@/run/redis/redis-server.sock
#
# The default account is disabled, so a client that does not sign in can
# do nothing. The helpdesk account may run only the commands the rate
# limiter uses, only on its own keys. This exact list was checked against
# the application with Redis 7.0: sign-in limiting and the readiness
# check work, while GET of other keys, SET, KEYS, FLUSHALL and CONFIG
# are refused. On Redis 7.2 or newer, also allow +client|setinfo.
#
# For administration, connect as root on the server with a separate,
# temporarily created account rather than giving the helpdesk more.

user default off
user helpdesk on >CHANGE-ME ~LIMITS:LIMITER/helpdesk/* resetchannels -@all +ping +get +incrby +expire +ttl +evalsha +eval +script|load +script|exists +hello +auth
